---
import Plate from '../../plate/Plate.astro';
import FilmControls from '../../plate/FilmControls.astro';
import FilmSubtitles from '../../plate/FilmSubtitles.astro';
import FilmTranscript from '../../plate/FilmTranscript.astro';
import '../../plate/film.css';
import { renderFormula } from '../../../lib/formulas/render';
import { createPartyModel, curveValue, type CurveKind } from './math';
import { CUES, TIMELINE } from './story';
import './style.css';

const model = createPartyModel();
const labels = [
  { id: 'r33', tex: String.raw`r(3,3)=6` },
  { id: 'rst', tex: String.raw`r(s,t)` },
  { id: 'r55', tex: String.raw`r(5,5)` },
  { id: 'classical', tex: String.raw`t^4` },
  { id: 'aks', tex: String.raw`\frac{t^4}{(\log t)^3}` },
  { id: 'bradac', tex: String.raw`\frac{t^4}{(\log t)^6}` },
  { id: 'spencer', tex: String.raw`\left(\frac{t}{\log t}\right)^3` },
  { id: 'curve-claim', tex: String.raw`\frac{t^4}{(\log t)^{3+\varepsilon}}` },
  { id: 'log-claim', tex: String.raw`(\log t)^{3+\varepsilon}` },
  { id: 'general-log', tex: String.raw`s-2+\varepsilon` },
  { id: 'flag-rule', tex: String.raw`\begin{gathered}i<j:\ a_i\perp b_j\\a_j\not\perp b_i\end{gathered}` },
  { id: 'entropy-lower', tex: String.raw`d\sigma\ell+\eta\ell\log\sigma` },
  { id: 'entropy-description', tex: String.raw`d\sigma\ell+O(k)` },
  { id: 'coarse', tex: String.raw`O(q\sigma^2)` },
] as const;
const people = Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, index) => {
  const angle = -Math.PI / 2 + index * Math.PI / 3;

  return { x: 250 + 77 * Math.cos(angle), y: 131 + 77 * Math.sin(angle) };
});
const partyLines = model.party.pairs.map(([a, b], index) => {
  const first = people[a];
  const second = people[b];
  const acquainted = model.party.colors[index];

  if (!first || !second || acquainted === undefined) throw new Error('Every static party pair has two people and a style.');

  return { first, second, acquainted };
});
const triangles = model.party.triangles.map(triangle => triangle.vertices.map(vertex => {
  const point = people[vertex];

  if (!point) throw new Error('Every highlighted triangle uses an existing person.');

  return `${point.x},${point.y}`;
}).join(' '));
const knownRows = [
  { s: 3, upper: model.ladder['3'].upper, lower: Number(model.ladder['3'].lower[0]?.exp), label: 'KIM 1995' },
  { s: 4, upper: model.ladder['4'].upper, lower: Number(model.ladder['4'].lower[1]?.exp), label: '2023' },
  { s: 5, upper: model.ladder['5'].upper, lower: Number(model.ladder['5'].lower[1]?.exp), label: 'BRADAČ 2026' },
];

if (knownRows.some(row => !Number.isFinite(row.lower))) throw new Error('The static ladder requires all three known numeric lower exponents.');

const ladderX = (exponent: number) => 105 + exponent * 58;
const plot = { x: 58, y: 52, w: 397, h: 149 };
const plotX = (logT: number) => plot.x + (logT - 2) / 7 * plot.w;
const plotY = (logR: number) => plot.y + plot.h * (1 - logR / 37);
const curvePoints = (kind: CurveKind) => Array.from({ length: 121 }, (_, index) => {
  const logT = 2 + index / 120 * 7;

  return `${plotX(logT).toFixed(3)},${plotY(Math.log10(curveValue(kind, 10 ** logT))).toFixed(3)}`;
});
const classical = curvePoints('classical');
const upper = curvePoints('aks');
const lower = curvePoints('bradac');
const band = upper.concat(lower.slice().reverse()).join(' ');
---

<Plate
  caption="Every way of pairing six people as friends or strangers hides a trio of one kind; five people need not. For fixed s and growing t, the bounds on r(s,t) differ only in the power of log t. Kim closed the gap for s = 3, Bradač found the power of t for every s, and the papers claim the logarithm's power is s − 2 for every s ≥ 5. The case s = 4 stays open."
  leftOut="Li, Rousseau and Zang's constant; Bohman and Keevash; Hermitian unitals; Mubayi and Verstraete; the Marking lemma; the Sparse-Pair Description, rich-line bounds and characteristic restriction; the Short-Row Description and Nie and Wang's inequality; the tree of windows, fresh validation and stage budgets; the reproved AKS bound; the diagonal numbers. The chart's heights and bit bars' lengths are schematic, and the finite-field graph is a toy."
>
  <uruk-party-gap class="film-host">
    <div class="pgfilm">
      <div class="pgfilm-stage" data-film-viewport>
        <canvas class="pgfilm-canvas" data-film-canvas role="img" aria-label="Six people and fifteen solid or dashed pairs reveal two acquainted trios. A ladder and logarithmic chart show the known gaps in off-diagonal Ramsey bounds. A small exact flag graph illustrates the construction, and schematic bit bars illustrate the claimed entropy contradiction. Blue marks identify the unreviewed claims. A full text transcript follows."></canvas>
        <div class="pgfilm-still" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="pgfilm-still-party" viewBox="0 0 500 250" role="presentation">
            <text x="250" y="23" text-anchor="middle" font-size="24">SIX PEOPLE · TWO ACQUAINTED TRIOS</text>
            {partyLines.map(edge => <line x1={edge.first.x} y1={edge.first.y} x2={edge.second.x} y2={edge.second.y} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray={edge.acquainted ? undefined : '7 5'} opacity=".6" />)}
            {triangles.map(points => <polygon points={points} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="4" />)}
            {people.map((person, index) => <g><circle cx={person.x} cy={person.y} r="11" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2" /><text x={person.x} y={person.y + 7} text-anchor="middle" font-size="21">{index + 1}</text></g>)}
            <text x="250" y="239" text-anchor="middle" font-size="22">SOLID FRIENDS · DASHED STRANGERS</text>
          </svg>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 500 250" role="presentation">
            <text x="250" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="25">POWER OF log t · KNOWN BOUNDS</text>
            <text x="250" y="44" text-anchor="middle" font-size="20">AKS UPPER TICKS · LOWER DOTS</text>
            {knownRows.map((row, index) => <g>
              <text x="20" y={84 + index * 54} font-size="24">s = {row.s}</text>
              <line x1={ladderX(0)} y1={78 + index * 54} x2={ladderX(6)} y2={78 + index * 54} stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1" />
              <rect x={ladderX(row.upper)} y={71 + index * 54} width={ladderX(row.lower) - ladderX(row.upper)} height="14" fill="var(--ink)" opacity=".15" />
              <line x1={ladderX(row.upper)} y1={67 + index * 54} x2={ladderX(row.upper)} y2={89 + index * 54} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="3" />
              <circle cx={ladderX(row.lower)} cy={78 + index * 54} r="5" fill="var(--ink)" />
              <text x={ladderX(row.lower)} y={62 + index * 54} text-anchor={row.s === 5 ? 'end' : 'middle'} font-size="21">{row.label}</text>
            </g>)}
            {[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6].map(value => <text x={ladderX(value)} y="224" text-anchor="middle" font-size="23">{value}</text>)}
          </svg>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 500 250" role="presentation">
            <text x="250" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="23">s = 5 · r AGAINST t · LOG AXES</text>
            <polygon points={band} fill="var(--ink)" opacity=".13" />
            <path d={`M${plot.x} ${plot.y}V${plot.y + plot.h}H${plot.x + plot.w}`} fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.2" />
            {[8, 16, 24, 32].map(value => <text class="pgfilm-still-math" x={plot.x - 10} y={plotY(value) + 5} text-anchor="end" font-size="19">10<tspan baseline-shift="super" font-size="14">{value}</tspan></text>)}
            {[2, 4, 6, 8, 9].map(value => <text class="pgfilm-still-math" x={plotX(value)} y="222" text-anchor="middle" font-size="19">10<tspan baseline-shift="super" font-size="14">{value}</tspan></text>)}
            <polyline points={classical.join(' ')} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.4" />
            <polyline points={upper.join(' ')} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2" />
            <polyline points={lower.join(' ')} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.7" />
            <text class="pgfilm-still-math" x="459" y="49" text-anchor="end" font-size="20">t⁴</text>
            <rect x="350" y="64" width="124" height="24" fill="var(--paper)" />
            <text x="468" y="82" text-anchor="end" font-size="20">AKS UPPER</text>
            <rect x="312" y="88" width="162" height="25" fill="var(--paper)" />
            <text x="468" y="106" text-anchor="end" font-size="20">BRADAČ LOWER</text>
            <text class="pgfilm-still-math" x="477" y="220" font-size="24">t</text>
            <text x="250" y="246" text-anchor="middle" font-size="20">CONSTANTS SET TO 1 · HEIGHTS SCHEMATIC</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="pgfilm-formulas" aria-hidden="true" data-bleed>
          {labels.map(label => <span class="pgfilm-label" data-label={label.id}><span set:html={renderFormula(label.tex, false)} /></span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="pgfilm-fallback-caption">Six people always contain a trio of friends or a trio of strangers. The known logarithmic-exponent gap is closed for s = 3, remains from 2 to 4 for s = 4, and runs from 3 to 6 for s = 5. This still shows the known bounds before the claim appears. The chart sets every constant to one.</p>
      <FilmSubtitles cues={CUES} />
    </div>
    <FilmControls id="pgfilm-timeline" timeline={TIMELINE} step={50} />
    <FilmTranscript cues={CUES}>
      <p class="film-method">How the film is made. The browser checks all {model.party.six.total.toLocaleString('en-US')} ways to colour the fifteen pairs of six people. Every one has a one-colour triangle. It also checks all {model.party.five.total.toLocaleString('en-US')} colourings of five people, of which {model.party.five.without} have no such triangle. The carried six-person sample comes from seed {model.party.huntSeed}. Its two one-colour triangles are the acquainted trios 1, 4, 5 and 2, 3, 6. Acquainted pairs are solid and stranger pairs are dashed, using one ink.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The chart evaluates the stated bound formulas on logarithmic axes, with every multiplicative constant set to one. Its heights and shaded bands illustrate growth rates and do not give numerical bounds at a particular party size. The ladder's exponents come from the article. Kim's row closes at one. The known rows for s = 4 and s = 5 retain their gaps. The blue marks identify the papers' claims, including the arbitrarily small positive logarithmic loss; their visible offset is schematic. The constant in the asymptotic result is still open.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The flag graph is an exact toy in the projective plane over the field with three elements, with {model.toy.points.length} points, {model.toy.points.length} lines and {model.toy.allFlags.length} incident flags. The twenty stored flags are sampled independently and uniformly in order. The browser rebuilds all {model.toy.graph.edges.length} edges using the one-way incidence rule, finds no triangle, and searches exactly for the largest independent set, which has {model.toy.independent.length} positions. The tag about {model.toy.streamsChecked.toLocaleString('en-US')} further streams reports the canonical script's check. The papers use dimension s − 1 and enormous fields. This toy does not show their scale or prove the claimed bound.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The independent group keeps its identities while it lifts out of the flag row. The two bit bars have schematic lengths. They illustrate the claimed entropy contradiction; they are not numerical entropy measurements of this twenty-flag example, and the drawing does not verify the argument. Bradač's coarser count is included as context for the logarithmic improvement.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The scope and review ledger follow the article. The claimed result fixes the logarithmic exponent for every fixed s at least five, leaves the constant open, and does not cover s = 4. As of 18 October 2026 no mathematician had publicly reported reading or checking the proofs. The two Lean comparator statements are outside the catalogue, and there is no outside replay. A formal statement is not counted as independent human approval.</p>
    </FilmTranscript>
  </uruk-party-gap>
</Plate>

<script>
  import './element';
</script>
